We now have a system of three equations with three unknowns. We can solve this system using various methods, such as substitution or elimination. Here, we will use the elimination method.

First, we subtract the second equation from the first equation:
\begin{align*}
(4a - 2b + c) - (a + b + c) &= 13 - (-2) \\
